    "lawCode": "Amd §13-0325, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S7216\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the environmental conservation law, in\nrelation to extending the authority of the department of environmental\nconservation to manage clams\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL: To extend the Department of\nEnvironmental Conservation's (DEC) authority to manage clams.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS: This bill would extend until December\n31, 2016, the DEC's authority to fix, by regulation, management\nmeasures for clams in State waters.\n\nJUSTIFICATION: This bill will extend the authority for DEC to regulate\nhard clams, soft or steamer clams and razor clams, including the\ndevelopment of long-term restoration strategies. Failure to extend\nDEC's existing regulatory authority by December 31, 2014 will result\nin a loss of, protections for these species.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY: Last extended by Chapter 481 of the Laws of\n2011.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: None to the State.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE: This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
